<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-RBQ-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-RBQ-001" ;
  triage:title "Task row/event SQL duplicated three times with no single owner" ;
  triage:description "The tasks/task_events SELECT text is maintained independently in task_store.rs:143-164,237-261,263-292 (SqliteTaskStore), task_ledger_reader.rs:75-132 (async reader lane) and writer/task_ops.rs:29-71 (writer transaction). writer/task_ops.rs filters state <> 'complete' in SQL with no ORDER BY while TaskStore::open_tasks filters and sorts in Rust, so the two open-task definitions already diverge in mechanism; no test or TOML keeps the copies in sync. Remediation: one crate-private query module (e.g. task_sql) exposing select_task_row / select_tasks_for_team / select_task_events over an explicit connection, reusing the existing decode_row/decode_event_row; all three call sites use it; add a task_store_boundary.rs assertion that the tasks/task_events column list appears exactly once in the crate." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "phase_end_review" ;
  triage:category "ruthless-boundary-qa" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
